## Motion, imagery and provider branding should become a system

### Motion should have levels

Google’s Material motion system now explicitly separates expressive hero motion from standard motion for recurring utility interactions. citeturn13view3

I would adopt the same conceptual distinction for TrueCost.

#### Micro motion

For:

```text
button press
chip selection
quantity stepper
favorite
provider selection
toggle
```

Suggested feel:

```text
120–180ms
small transform
opacity
subtle haptic where meaningful
```

#### Structural motion

For:

```text
bottom sheet
screen section transition
filter expansion
card expansion
comparison reveal
```

Suggested feel:

```text
220–360ms
controlled spring
opacity + translation
```

#### Signature expressive motion

Reserved for:

```text
TrueCost search activation
recommendation reveal
basket optimization completion
flight route reveal
mobility route reveal
major success state
```

Suggested feel:

```text
400–650ms
carefully tuned spring / staged choreography
```

The exact numbers are a proposed TrueCost motion specification, not platform requirements.

The crucial rule:

> **Only one element on a screen should usually be doing expressive motion at a time.**

### The best recommendation animation

Suppose TrueCost compares four grocery baskets.

Do not do this:

```text
confetti
coins flying
four cards bouncing
glowing border pulsing forever
price spinning
logo rotating
```

Do this:

```text
provider cards appear softly
      ↓
totals count into final values
      ↓
non-winners settle slightly
      ↓
winner lifts 4–6px
      ↓
TrueCost iris edge appears
      ↓
"Save ₹77" fades/slides in
      ↓
single light haptic
```

Then everything becomes still.

The user receives the emotional “decision completed” moment without the app becoming exhausting.

### Use Reanimated for interface motion

The current Reanimated documentation recommends the maintained Reanimated 4 line where compatible with the project architecture and specifically notes that non-layout properties such as `transform` and `opacity` are generally more performant than repeatedly animating width, height, margin, top, or left. It also warns against animating excessive numbers of independent components simultaneously. citeturn15search2turn15search7

Therefore:

```text
Reanimated
→ 90% of interface movement

Rive
→ a few premium branded interactive illustrations

Skia
→ genuinely complex custom visualizations/effects
```

Not:

```text
Rive animation on every card
Skia on every page
40 looping Lotties
```

Rive state machines are useful for a branded interactive object because they can transition based on inputs and can settle when there is nothing left to animate, reducing unnecessary ongoing work. citeturn14search0

React Native Skia can integrate directly with Reanimated for more complex UI-thread animations, while its Skottie component can render Lottie animation content with programmatic control. citeturn14search1turn14search3

