Apple recommends high-resolution image assets and maintaining the intended image aspect ratio; it also recommends testing images across real devices rather than assuming the design-tool preview is sufficient. citeturn17search0turn17search2

TrueCost should establish a strict image hierarchy:

**Level A — exact source imagery.**

Use for:

```text
Grocery products
Shopping products
Medicine packaging
Restaurant dishes
Hotels where relevant
Provider-authorized imagery
```

Only where the image is tied to the actual entity.

**Level B — editorial/category imagery.**

Use for:

```text
Travel hero
Food discovery
Home/onboarding
Category transitions
```

These should communicate emotion rather than pretend to represent the exact item.

**Level C — custom TrueCost illustration.**

Use for:

```text
empty states
no exact match
comparison unavailable
savings explanation
privacy
onboarding
