### Accessibility cannot be the “boring version”

Apple recommends controls at least 44×44 points, while Android recommends touch targets of at least 48×48dp for touch interfaces. citeturn17search0turn15search6

WCAG’s minimum text contrast is 4.5:1 for normal-size text and 3:1 for sufficiently large text. citeturn19search0

And Apple specifically recommends adapting animations when Reduce Motion is enabled: large translations and depth simulations can be replaced by fades/highlights, springs can be tightened, and animated blur/depth effects should be avoided for affected users. citeturn15search0turn15search4

So:

```text
Default:
card rises + transitions + subtle blur

Reduce Motion:
crossfade + highlight
```

That is still beautiful.

### Edge-to-edge should be part of the redesign

Android’s current guidance recommends drawing visual backgrounds and scrolling content edge-to-edge while protecting interactive content from system bars, cutouts and gesture regions. citeturn16search0turn16search7

TrueCost’s travel hero, maps, imagery and category backgrounds should take advantage of this.

Important text/buttons should remain inset.

This will make the app feel far more modern than the common pattern:

```text
opaque status bar
↓
rectangular toolbar
↓
card stack
↓
opaque navigation bar
```

## The redesign program I would use on the real TrueCost codebase

Do **not** tell a coding agent:

> “Make everything beautiful.”

That leads to random gradients, inconsistent components and a big unreviewable rewrite.

The redesign should be executed as a controlled product-design program.

### Discovery and visual baseline

Before code changes:

```text
Inventory every mobile screen
Inventory every reusable component
Inventory navigation
Inventory current fonts
Inventory colors
Inventory animation packages
Inventory image packages
Inventory current provider logos
Inventory empty/loading/error states
Inventory category-specific components
```

Then run the emulator and screenshot every meaningful existing screen.

Create:

```text
artifacts/ui_redesign/before/
```

This gives us objective before/after evidence.

Because your own repository audit shows that backend feature depth is currently different across categories, design must also distinguish fully backed experiences from categories/providers that are replay-only, connector-only, blocked, or incomplete. A beautiful screen must not visually imply live coverage that the system cannot actually provide. fileciteturn0file0

